  "title": "2026-07-29-eval-202743 · ivr-agent-handoff",
  "description": "# Phone support with AI agent handoff\n\nThis diagram shows the inbound-call journey from caller-number lookup through greeting, consent, intent capture, AI self-service, and human escalation.\n\n- **Identity and greeting:** ANI drives a customer lookup; matched callers receive a personalized greeting, while failed or unmatched lookups receive a generic greeting.\n- **Consent and intent:** recording/transcription consent is captured before a speech-first menu identifies intent, with keypad fallback when recognition is unreliable.\n- **AI self-service:** routine intents go to the AI voice agent, which reads account facts through a read-only service and uses only authorized actions.\n- **Human handoff:** unresolved requests, explicit requests for a person, and low-confidence risk flags enter the human queue with transcript, account context, intent, and completed work. A support agent takes the call within target, or the caller is offered a callback.\n- **Quality loop:** recordings and transcripts from unresolved or abandoned calls are reviewed, and the resulting policy adjusts which intents the AI may handle.\n\nRead left to right across the upper flow, then downward into greeting, quality review, or human handoff branches; the dashed orange connection is the policy feedback loop.",
